(function(E){ const x = E["exam-02"] = E["exam-02"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x02-r1"] = {"id":"x02-r1","patterns":["RA-nature","GT1-notices","GT1-reviews","PARA-cause","PARA-rules"],"title":{"en":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","tr":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","fa":"Reading ۱: متن ۱ (Passage 1) / بخش ۱ (Section 1)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete a table with single words from a science passage and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN, paying attention to careful words such as \"may\" and \"suggests\".","tr":"Bu derste bir bilim metnindeki tek kelimelerle bir tabloyu tamamlamayı ve \"may\", \"suggests\" gibi temkinli kelimelere dikkat ederek TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یک جدول را با تک‌کلمه‌هایی از یک متن علمی کامل کنی و با توجه به کلمه‌های محتاطانه مثل «may» و «suggests» بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to check statements against an everyday notice (TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN), and to match facts to five short listings when one letter can be used more than once.","tr":"Bu derste ifadeleri günlük bir duyuruyla karşılaştırmayı (TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN) ve bir harfin birden fazla kullanılabildiği durumda bilgileri beş kısa ilanla eşleştirmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌ها را با یک اطلاعیه‌ی روزمره مقایسه کنی (TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN) و اطلاعات را به پنج معرفی کوتاه وصل کنی، وقتی یک حرف می‌تواند بیش از یک بار بیاید."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 1: a science report","tr":"Reading Passage 1: bir bilim yazısı","fa":"Reading Passage 1: یک گزارش علمی"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to complete a table with single words from a science passage and to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN, paying attention to careful words such as \"may\" and \"suggests\".","tr":"Bu derste bir bilim metnindeki tek kelimelerle bir tabloyu tamamlamayı ve \"may\", \"suggests\" gibi temkinli kelimelere dikkat ederek TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری یک جدول را با تک‌کلمه‌هایی از یک متن علمی کامل کنی و با توجه به کلمه‌های محتاطانه مثل «may» و «suggests» بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}},{"label":{"en":"Words","tr":"Kelime","fa":"کلمه"},"value":"~800"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: can plants hear?","tr":"Bu sınav: bitkiler duyabilir mi?","fa":"این آزمون: آیا گیاهان می‌شنوند؟"},"intro":{"en":"Academic Passage 1 is often a clear report on the natural world. Here it describes experiments one by one, so the table follows the experiments. Learn the paraphrases first: the table and the statements use other words.","tr":"Academic Passage 1 çoğu zaman doğa hakkında açık bir rapordur. Burada deneyleri tek tek anlatıyor; tablo da deneyleri izliyor. Önce eş anlamlıları öğren: tablo ve ifadeler başka kelimeler kullanır.","fa":"Academic Passage 1 اغلب گزارشی روشن درباره‌ی طبیعت است. این‌جا آزمایش‌ها را یکی‌یکی توضیح می‌دهد، پس جدول هم دنبال آزمایش‌ها می‌آید. اول معادل‌ها را یاد بگیر: جدول و جمله‌ها کلمه‌های دیگری به کار می‌برند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x02-r1-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-nature","PARA-cause"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"Plants and sound","tr":"Bitkiler ve ses","fa":"گیاهان و صدا"},"asks":{"en":"A science article that reports several experiments, one after another: what each team did, what the plants did, and how careful scientists are about the results. Passage 1 is often about nature, with a table or notes and TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Birkaç deneyi art arda aktaran bir bilim yazısı: her ekibin ne yaptığı, bitkilerin nasıl tepki verdiği ve bilim insanlarının sonuçlar konusunda ne kadar temkinli olduğu. Passage 1 çoğu zaman doğa hakkındadır; bir tablo ya da notlar ve TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN ile gelir.","fa":"یک مقاله‌ی علمی که چند آزمایش را پشت سر هم گزارش می‌کند: هر گروه چه کرد، گیاه‌ها چه واکنشی نشان دادند و دانشمندها درباره‌ی نتیجه‌ها چقدر محتاط‌اند. Passage 1 اغلب درباره‌ی طبیعت است، با یک جدول یا یادداشت و TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN."},"fields":["Old experiments","Why plants might hear","Experiment 1: leaves","Experiment 2: roots","Experiment 3: flowers","Plants making sounds","Doubts","Possible uses"],"words":[{"a":"vibration","b":"a fast movement / a shaking","tr":"titreşim","fa":"لرزش"},{"a":"detect","b":"sense / pick up","tr":"algılamak","fa":"تشخیص دادن، حس کردن"},{"a":"respond to","b":"react to","tr":"tepki vermek","fa":"واکنش نشان دادن به"},{"a":"defensive","b":"that protects against attack","tr":"savunmaya yönelik","fa":"دفاعی"},{"a":"seedling","b":"a very young plant","tr":"fide","fa":"نهال"},{"a":"moist","b":"slightly wet / damp","tr":"nemli","fa":"نمناک"},{"a":"pollinator","b":"an insect that carries pollen","tr":"tozlayıcı","fa":"گرده‌افشان"},{"a":"roughly","b":"about / approximately","tr":"yaklaşık","fa":"تقریباً"},{"a":"striking","b":"surprising / remarkable","tr":"çarpıcı","fa":"چشمگیر"},{"a":"thirsty","b":"short of water / left without water","tr":"susuz","fa":"تشنه، بی‌آب"},{"a":"criticise","b":"say something is wrong","tr":"eleştirmek","fa":"انتقاد کردن"},{"a":"tested on farms","b":"tried out in real fields","tr":"çiftliklerde denenmiş","fa":"در مزرعه آزمایش‌شده"}],"traps":[{"en":"Hedges: the passage says \"may\", \"appeared to\" or \"suggests\". A statement that says something was proved is not the same.","tr":"Temkinli ifadeler: metin \"may\", \"appeared to\" ya da \"suggests\" der. Bir şeyin kanıtlandığını söyleyen ifade aynı şey değildir.","fa":"کلمه‌های احتیاط: متن می‌گوید «may»، «appeared to» یا «suggests». جمله‌ای که می‌گوید چیزی ثابت شده، با این یکی نیست."},{"en":"One team’s result is not every team’s result. If the passage reports one study, a statement about other teams repeating it is usually NOT GIVEN.","tr":"Bir ekibin sonucu her ekibin sonucu değildir. Metin tek bir çalışmayı anlatıyorsa, başka ekiplerin onu tekrarladığını söyleyen ifade genelde NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"نتیجه‌ی یک گروه نتیجه‌ی همه‌ی گروه‌ها نیست. اگر متن یک پژوهش را گزارش کند، جمله‌ای درباره‌ی تکرارش توسط گروه‌های دیگر معمولاً NOT GIVEN است."},{"en":"The table uses short labels, but the answer word is copied from the passage in the same form.","tr":"Tablo kısa etiketler kullanır ama cevap kelimesi metinden aynı biçimde kopyalanır.","fa":"جدول برچسب‌های کوتاه دارد، اما کلمه‌ی جواب با همان شکل از متن کپی می‌شود."}],"example":{"text":"\"Sunflower seedlings turned towards a lamp within an hour, and they turned back again when the lamp was switched off.\"","item":"Statement: The sunflower seedlings turned faster than other plants. TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","answer":"NOT GIVEN","why":{"en":"The text gives the time for sunflowers only. There is nothing to compare with other plants.","tr":"Metin yalnızca ayçiçekleri için süreyi veriyor. Başka bitkilerle karşılaştıracak bir bilgi yok.","fa":"متن فقط زمانِ آفتابگردان‌ها را می‌دهد. چیزی برای مقایسه با گیاهان دیگر نیست."}}},{"id":"RA-nature-p1","ctx":["RA-nature"],"title":{"en":"Natural history accounts","tr":"Doğa tarihi anlatıları","fa":"روایت‌های تاریخ طبیعی"},"asks":{"en":"A factual account of an animal, a plant or a natural place: how it lives, how it was discovered, why it declined and how it is protected. Statements test single facts; the notes follow the order of the text.","tr":"Bir hayvan, bitki ya da doğal bir yer hakkında bilgilendirici bir metin: nasıl yaşadığı, nasıl keşfedildiği, neden azaldığı ve nasıl korunduğu. İfadeler tek tek bilgileri sınar; notlar metnin sırasını izler.","fa":"متنی اطلاعاتی درباره‌ی یک حیوان، یک گیاه یا یک مکان طبیعی: چطور زندگی می‌کند، چطور کشف شد، چرا کم شد و چطور از آن حفاظت می‌شود. جمله‌ها اطلاعات جزئی را می‌سنجند؛ یادداشت‌ها ترتیب متن را دنبال می‌کنند."},"fields":["The species was first described in the 1800s.","Its numbers have fallen since the 1950s.","It is found only on one island.","Farmers consider it a pest.","Notes: Diet · Habitat · Threats · Protection"],"words":[{"a":"declined","b":"fell in number / became scarcer","tr":"azaldı","fa":"کم شد"},{"a":"disappeared","b":"became extinct / died out","tr":"yok oldu","fa":"از بین رفت"},{"a":"only","b":"exclusively / nowhere else","tr":"yalnızca","fa":"فقط"},{"a":"first","b":"the earliest / originally","tr":"ilk","fa":"اولین"},{"a":"increased","b":"rose / grew / expanded","tr":"arttı","fa":"افزایش یافت"},{"a":"protect","b":"conserve / save from","tr":"korumak","fa":"حفاظت کردن"},{"a":"harmful","b":"damaging / a threat to","tr":"zararlı","fa":"مضر"},{"a":"common","b":"widespread / found in many places","tr":"yaygın","fa":"رایج"},{"a":"scientists","b":"researchers / biologists","tr":"bilim insanları","fa":"دانشمندان"},{"a":"uncertain","b":"it remains unclear / not yet known","tr":"belirsiz","fa":"نامعلوم"},{"a":"caused by","b":"the result of / due to","tr":"... yüzünden","fa":"ناشی از"},{"a":"brought in","b":"introduced by humans","tr":"dışarıdan getirilmiş","fa":"وارد شده"}],"traps":[{"en":"Hedging: \"may\", \"some researchers believe\". A statement that turns this into a fact is usually FALSE or NOT GIVEN; compare carefully.","tr":"Temkinli dil: \"may\", \"bazı araştırmacılara göre\". Bunu kesin bilgiye çeviren bir ifade genelde FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN olur; dikkatle karşılaştır.","fa":"زبان محتاطانه: «may»، «بعضی پژوهشگرها معتقدند». جمله‌ای که این را به واقعیت قطعی تبدیل کند معمولاً FALSE یا NOT GIVEN است؛ دقیق مقایسه کن."},{"en":"\"Only\", \"always\", \"never\" in a statement: one exception in the text makes it FALSE.","tr":"İfadede \"only\", \"always\", \"never\": metindeki tek bir istisna onu FALSE yapar.","fa":"«only»، «always»، «never» در جمله: یک استثنا در متن آن را FALSE می‌کند."},{"en":"Notes: two numbers or dates sit close together. The heading decides which one you need.","tr":"Notlar: iki sayı ya da tarih yan yanadır. Hangisinin gerektiğine başlık karar verir.","fa":"یادداشت‌ها: دو عدد یا تاریخ نزدیک هم‌اند. عنوان تعیین می‌کند کدام را لازم داری."}],"example":{"text":"The hazel dormouse was once found in woods across most of England. Its range has shrunk by about half since 1900, mainly because the hedges that linked woodlands were removed. Most surviving populations are now in the south.","item":"Statement: The dormouse has always lived only in the south of England.  (TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"Once found in woods across most of England\" contradicts \"always... only in the south\".","tr":"\"Bir zamanlar İngiltere’nin çoğunda\" bulunması, \"her zaman... yalnızca güneyde\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«زمانی در جنگل‌های بیشتر انگلستان بود» با «همیشه... فقط در جنوب» در تضاد است."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-nature"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-nature","n":37,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 37 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 37’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۳۷ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"A table, then eight statements","tr":"Bir tablo, sonra sekiz ifade","fa":"یک جدول، بعد هشت جمله"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-5: complete a table with ONE WORD ONLY from the passage. Questions 6-13: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN. The table follows the order of the experiments, and the statements follow the order of the passage.","tr":"Soru 1-5: tabloyu metinden YALNIZCA BİR KELİMEYLE tamamla. Soru 6-13: TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN. Tablo deneylerin sırasını, ifadeler de metnin sırasını izler.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۵: جدول را فقط با یک کلمه از متن کامل کن. سؤال‌های ۶ تا ۱۳: TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN. جدول ترتیب آزمایش‌ها و جمله‌ها ترتیب متن را دنبال می‌کنند."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Row by row, then line by line","tr":"Önce satır satır, sonra cümle cümle","fa":"اول ردیف به ردیف، بعد جمله به جمله"},"steps":[{"en":"Use the first column of the table (the plant) to find the right paragraph.","tr":"Doğru paragrafı bulmak için tablonun ilk sütununu (bitki) kullan.","fa":"برای پیدا کردن پاراگراف درست از ستون اول جدول (گیاه) استفاده کن."},{"en":"Read the words around the gap, find them in other words, and copy one word exactly.","tr":"Boşluğun etrafındaki kelimeleri oku, başka kelimelerle söylenmiş hâlini bul ve tek kelimeyi aynen kopyala.","fa":"کلمه‌های دور جای خالی را بخوان، معادلشان را در متن پیدا کن و یک کلمه را دقیقاً کپی کن."},{"en":"For each statement, find the sentence it is about and check every detail, including how certain it is.","tr":"Her ifade için ilgili cümleyi bul ve her ayrıntıyı, ne kadar kesin olduğu da dahil, kontrol et.","fa":"برای هر جمله، جمله‌ی مربوط در متن را پیدا کن و همه‌ی جزئیات، از جمله میزان قطعیتش را، چک کن."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","tr":"FALSE mı NOT GIVEN mı?","fa":"FALSE یا NOT GIVEN؟"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The text","The answer"],"tr":["Metin","Cevap"],"fa":["متن","جواب"]},"rows":[["says the same thing in other words","TRUE"],["says the opposite, or a different fact on the same point","FALSE"],["says nothing about this point","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One statement, step by step","tr":"Bir ifade, adım adım","fa":"یک جمله، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in the passage?","text":"\"The birds did not react to recordings of traffic, but they flew away at once when they heard the call of a hawk.\"","item":"Statement: The birds reacted to every sound they heard.","answer":"FALSE","walk":[{"en":"Find the place: the sentence about recordings.","tr":"Yeri bul: kayıtlarla ilgili cümle.","fa":"جایش را پیدا کن: جمله‌ای که درباره‌ی ضبط‌هاست."},{"en":"Compare: \"did not react to recordings of traffic\".","tr":"Karşılaştır: \"trafik kayıtlarına tepki vermediler\".","fa":"مقایسه کن: «به صدای ضبط‌شده‌ی ترافیک واکنش نشان ندادند»."},{"en":"\"Every sound\" is contradicted: FALSE, not NOT GIVEN.","tr":"\"Her ses\" ile çelişiyor: NOT GIVEN değil, FALSE.","fa":"«هر صدایی» نقض می‌شود: FALSE، نه NOT GIVEN."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"The results suggest that the frogs may use sound to find water.\" Statement: \"Scientists have proved that frogs find water by sound.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["TRUE","NOT GIVEN","FALSE"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"Suggest\" and \"may\" mean it is not proved, so \"have proved\" goes against the text.","tr":"\"Suggest\" ve \"may\" kanıtlanmadığını gösterir; \"kanıtladılar\" metinle çelişir.","fa":"«suggest» و «may» یعنی ثابت نشده، پس «ثابت کرده‌اند» با متن تناقض دارد."}},"remember":{"en":"Copy table answers exactly. For statements, check the facts and how sure the writer is.","tr":"Tablo cevaplarını aynen kopyala. İfadelerde gerçekleri ve yazarın ne kadar emin olduğunu kontrol et.","fa":"جواب‌های جدول را دقیقاً کپی کن. در جمله‌ها، واقعیت‌ها و میزان اطمینان نویسنده را چک کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x02-r1-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 1","title":{"en":"Can plants hear?","tr":"Bitkiler duyabilir mi?","fa":"آیا گیاهان می‌شنوند؟"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-nature"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.","passage":"Can plants hear?\n\nMany gardeners talk to their plants, and some play them music, convinced that it helps them grow. For most of the twentieth century, scientists regarded such ideas as harmless folklore. There was a reason for their doubts: the experiments that seemed to support them were often badly designed. They used a handful of plants, had no proper comparison group, and rarely controlled for light, temperature or water. When stricter studies failed to find any effect, the whole subject was quietly dropped.\n\nOver the last two decades, however, the question has returned in a more careful form. Sound, after all, is simply vibration travelling through air, water or solid material, and plants are already known to be highly sensitive to touch and movement. The leaves of some species fold up within seconds when they are brushed, and climbing plants coil around a support once they make contact with it. From an evolutionary point of view, it would be surprising if organisms that cannot move had not developed some way of using the information carried by vibrations, whether that information concerns an approaching insect, a passing pollinator or nearby water.\n\nOne of the first studies to take this idea seriously was carried out in the United States on thale cress, a small plant that is widely used in laboratory research. The researchers recorded the tiny vibrations produced by a caterpillar as it chewed a leaf, and then played these recordings back to other plants through the leaves themselves. When those plants were later attacked by real caterpillars, they produced larger amounts of defensive chemicals than plants that had been kept in silence. Just as important, the plants did not react in this way to vibrations made by wind, or to the call of an insect with a similar pitch. They appeared to be responding to the particular pattern of a feeding caterpillar.\n\nA second line of research has looked at roots. In an experiment in Australia, pea seedlings were grown in pots divided into two arms, so that each root system had to choose a direction. When the sound of water flowing through a pipe was played beside one arm, the roots tended to grow towards it, even though the soil around them was dry. When the soil on one side was actually moist, however, the roots grew towards the moisture rather than the sound. The researchers concluded that sound may help a plant to locate water at a distance, while moisture guides it over the final few centimetres.\n\nPerhaps the most striking results have come from flowers. A team in Israel exposed evening primrose plants to recordings of a bee's wingbeat. Within about three minutes, the sugar content of the plants' nectar had risen by roughly a fifth, so that the nectar became sweeter. Higher-pitched sounds produced no change, and neither did silence. Using a laser device, the team also showed that the petals themselves vibrated in response to the bee's sound, which suggests that the bowl-shaped flower may work rather like an ear. Sweeter nectar, they argued, could encourage a visiting bee to stay longer or to return, which would help the plant to spread its pollen.\n\nIf plants can detect sound, can they also produce it? In 2023 the same research group placed microphones near tomato and tobacco plants in a greenhouse. Plants that had been left without water, or whose stems had been cut, gave off short clicking sounds, too high for human ears to detect, at a rate of several dozen an hour. Healthy plants clicked far less often, typically less than once an hour. A computer program trained on the recordings was even able to tell whether a plant was thirsty or had been cut.\n\nResearchers are careful about what these findings mean. Nobody yet knows whether any animal listens to these clicks, although some insects can hear sounds in this range. The clicks may not be signals at all: one explanation is that they are caused by air bubbles forming in the narrow tubes that carry water up the stem when a plant is short of water. Several scientists have criticised newspaper headlines claiming that plants \"scream\", arguing that such language suggests feelings for which there is no evidence.\n\nThe practical possibilities are nevertheless attracting interest. Farmers might one day place cheap microphones among their crops and water only those plants that are clicking, saving water in dry regions. Growers might even play recorded wingbeats to flowering crops to increase their attractiveness to pollinators. Neither idea has yet been tested on working farms, and both would need to prove that they are cheaper than existing methods. Still, a subject that was once a joke has become a serious field of research.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 1-5. Complete the table below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 1-5 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"table","table":{"title":"Experiments on plants and sound","headers":["Plant","Sound or situation","Response"],"rows":[["thale cress","recorded vibrations of a (1) ___ eating a leaf","produced more defensive (2) ___ when later attacked"],["pea","(3) ___ flowing through a pipe","roots grew towards the sound"],["evening primrose","recording of a bee’s wingbeat","nectar became (4) ___ within about three minutes"],["tomato and tobacco","left without water, or stems (5) ___","short, very high clicks"]]},"questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"gap","prompt":"thale cress · Sound: recorded vibrations of a ___ eating a leaf","accept":["caterpillar"],"limit":1,"evidence":"the tiny vibrations produced by a caterpillar as it chewed a leaf","why":{"en":"\"Vibrations produced by a caterpillar as it chewed a leaf\": chewed = eating.","tr":"\"Bir tırtılın yaprağı çiğnerken çıkardığı titreşimler\": chewed = eating.","fa":"«لرزش‌هایی که یک کرمِ پروانه هنگام جویدن برگ ایجاد می‌کرد»: chewed یعنی خوردن."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-limit"]},{"n":2,"kind":"gap","prompt":"thale cress · Response: produced more defensive ___ when later attacked","accept":["chemicals"],"limit":1,"evidence":"larger amounts of defensive chemicals","why":{"en":"\"Larger amounts of defensive chemicals\" = more. Keep the plural.","tr":"\"Daha fazla miktarda savunma kimyasalı\" = more. Çoğulu koru.","fa":"«مقدار بیشتری از مواد شیمیایی دفاعی» یعنی more. جمع را نگه دار."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":3,"kind":"gap","prompt":"pea · Sound: ___ flowing through a pipe","accept":["water"],"limit":1,"evidence":"the sound of water flowing through a pipe","why":{"en":"\"The sound of water flowing through a pipe was played beside one arm.\"","tr":"\"Borudan akan suyun sesi bir kolun yanında çalındı.\"","fa":"«صدای آبی که از یک لوله می‌گذشت کنار یکی از شاخه‌ها پخش شد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":4,"kind":"gap","prompt":"evening primrose · Response: nectar became ___ within about three minutes","accept":["sweeter"],"limit":1,"evidence":"the nectar became sweeter","why":{"en":"The sugar content rose by about a fifth, \"so that the nectar became sweeter\".","tr":"Şeker oranı yaklaşık beşte bir arttı, \"böylece nektar daha tatlı oldu\".","fa":"قندِ شهد حدود یک‌پنجم بیشتر شد، «به‌طوری که شهد شیرین‌تر شد»."},"trap":["TR-limit"]},{"n":5,"kind":"gap","prompt":"tomato and tobacco · Situation: left without water, or stems ___","accept":["cut"],"limit":1,"evidence":"or whose stems had been cut","why":{"en":"\"Plants that had been left without water, or whose stems had been cut\".","tr":"\"Susuz bırakılmış ya da gövdeleri kesilmiş bitkiler\".","fa":"«گیاهانی که بی‌آب مانده بودند یا ساقه‌شان بریده شده بود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 6-13. Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 6-13 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":6,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Many early studies of music and plant growth were poorly planned.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"the experiments that seemed to support them were often badly designed","why":{"en":"\"Often badly designed\" = poorly planned.","tr":"\"Çoğu zaman kötü tasarlanmış\" = poorly planned.","fa":"«اغلب بد طراحی شده بودند» یعنی poorly planned."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":7,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The thale cress plants reacted to wind vibrations in the same way as to caterpillar vibrations.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"the plants did not react in this way to vibrations made by wind","why":{"en":"\"The plants did not react in this way to vibrations made by wind.\"","tr":"\"Bitkiler rüzgârın oluşturduğu titreşimlere bu şekilde tepki vermedi.\"","fa":"«گیاه‌ها به لرزش‌های باد این‌طور واکنش نشان ندادند»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":8,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Other research teams have obtained the same results with thale cress.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"One of the first studies to take this idea seriously","why":{"en":"The passage describes one study. It says nothing about other teams repeating it.","tr":"Metin tek bir çalışmayı anlatıyor. Başka ekiplerin onu tekrarladığına dair bir şey yok.","fa":"متن یک پژوهش را توصیف می‌کند. درباره‌ی تکرارش توسط گروه‌های دیگر چیزی نمی‌گوید."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":9,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"When the soil was wet on one side, the pea roots grew towards the wetness rather than the sound.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"the roots grew towards the moisture rather than the sound","why":{"en":"Moist soil = wet. \"The roots grew towards the moisture rather than the sound.\"","tr":"Nemli toprak = ıslak. \"Kökler sesten çok neme doğru büyüdü.\"","fa":"خاکِ نمناک یعنی خیس. «ریشه‌ها به سمت رطوبت رشد کردند، نه صدا»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":10,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The evening primrose flowers reacted to every sound that was played to them.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"Higher-pitched sounds produced no change","why":{"en":"\"Higher-pitched sounds produced no change, and neither did silence.\"","tr":"\"Daha tiz sesler hiçbir değişiklik yaratmadı, sessizlik de.\"","fa":"«صداهای زیرتر هیچ تغییری ایجاد نکردند، سکوت هم همین‌طور»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":11,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Bees prefer evening primrose flowers to other flowers.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"could encourage a visiting bee to stay longer or to return","why":{"en":"Sweeter nectar \"could\" make a bee stay or return. Nothing compares evening primrose with other flowers.","tr":"Daha tatlı nektar arının kalmasını ya da geri gelmesini \"sağlayabilir\". Çuha çiçeğini başka çiçeklerle karşılaştıran bir bilgi yok.","fa":"شهد شیرین‌تر «ممکن است» زنبور را نگه دارد یا برگرداند. هیچ مقایسه‌ای با گل‌های دیگر نیست."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge"]},{"n":12,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Plants that were short of water clicked more often than healthy plants.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"Healthy plants clicked far less often","why":{"en":"Thirsty or cut plants clicked \"several dozen\" times an hour; healthy plants \"far less often\".","tr":"Susuz ya da kesilmiş bitkiler saatte \"birkaç düzine\" kez tıkırdadı; sağlıklı bitkiler \"çok daha seyrek\".","fa":"گیاهانِ تشنه یا بریده ساعتی «چند ده» بار صدا دادند؛ گیاهان سالم «خیلی کمتر»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","PARA-cause"]},{"n":13,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Farmers already use microphones to decide which plants need water.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"Neither idea has yet been tested on working farms","why":{"en":"\"Might one day\" and \"neither idea has yet been tested on working farms\".","tr":"\"Bir gün ... olabilir\" ve \"iki fikir de henüz gerçek çiftliklerde denenmedi\".","fa":"«شاید روزی» و «هیچ‌کدام از این دو ایده هنوز در مزرعه‌های واقعی آزمایش نشده»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge"]}]}],"id":"c-x02-r1-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A table says \"an insect that carries pollen\". Which word would you look for in a passage?","options":["predator","pollinator","parasite"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A pollinator carries pollen from flower to flower.","tr":"Pollinator, poleni çiçekten çiçeğe taşır.","fa":"pollinator گرده را از گلی به گل دیگر می‌برد."}},{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The plants gave off clicking sounds.\" Here, \"gave off\" means...","options":["produced","received","stopped"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"To give off a sound, smell or light is to produce it.","tr":"Bir ses, koku ya da ışığı give off etmek, onu üretmektir.","fa":"give off کردنِ صدا، بو یا نور یعنی تولیدش کردن."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Table: \"seeds stored in ___ conditions\" (ONE WORD ONLY). The passage says \"the seeds were kept in very dry conditions\". What do you write?","options":["very dry","dryness","dry"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"One word, copied in the same form: dry.","tr":"Tek kelime, aynı biçimde kopyalanmış: dry.","fa":"یک کلمه، با همان شکل کپی‌شده: dry."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Only one team has carried out this experiment so far.\" Statement: \"Several teams have repeated the experiment.\"","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"\"Only one team... so far\" contradicts \"several teams\".","tr":"\"Şimdiye kadar yalnızca bir ekip\", \"birkaç ekip\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«تا حالا فقط یک گروه» با «چند گروه» تناقض دارد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"The beans grew taller under blue light.\" Statement: \"The beans grew taller under blue light than any other crop in the study.\"","options":["NOT GIVEN","TRUE","FALSE"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The text does not compare the beans with other crops.","tr":"Metin fasulyeleri başka ürünlerle karşılaştırmıyor.","fa":"متن لوبیاها را با محصول‌های دیگر مقایسه نمی‌کند."}}],"id":"c-x02-r1-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r1"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 1: a charter and listings","tr":"GT Reading Section 1: bir taahhütname ve ilanlar","fa":"GT Reading Section 1: یک تعهدنامه و چند معرفی"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to check statements against an everyday notice (TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN), and to match facts to five short listings when one letter can be used more than once.","tr":"Bu derste ifadeleri günlük bir duyuruyla karşılaştırmayı (TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN) ve bir harfin birden fazla kullanılabildiği durumda bilgileri beş kısa ilanla eşleştirmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری جمله‌ها را با یک اطلاعیه‌ی روزمره مقایسه کنی (TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN) و اطلاعات را به پنج معرفی کوتاه وصل کنی، وقتی یک حرف می‌تواند بیش از یک بار بیاید."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Letters","tr":"Harfler","fa":"حرف‌ها"},"value":"A-E"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: a pool and places to eat","tr":"Bu sınav: bir havuz ve yemek yerleri","fa":"این آزمون: یک استخر و جاهای غذاخوری"},"intro":{"en":"Section 1 has short texts from daily life. Notices and rules come up often, and so do short descriptions or reviews of places. The questions test exact details: who, when, how much, and what is allowed.","tr":"Section 1 günlük hayattan kısa metinler içerir. Duyurular ve kurallar sık çıkar, yerlerin kısa tanıtımları ya da yorumları da. Sorular kesin ayrıntıları ölçer: kim, ne zaman, ne kadar ve neye izin var.","fa":"Section 1 متن‌های کوتاهی از زندگی روزمره دارد. اطلاعیه‌ها و قانون‌ها زیاد می‌آیند و معرفی یا نظرهای کوتاه درباره‌ی مکان‌ها هم همین‌طور. سؤال‌ها جزئیات دقیق را می‌سنجند: چه کسی، کی، چقدر و چه چیزی مجاز است."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x02-r1gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT1-notices","GT1-reviews","PARA-rules"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-notices","n":22,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 22 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 22’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۲ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A pool charter and five places to eat","tr":"Bir havuz taahhütnamesi ve beş yemek yeri","fa":"تعهدنامه‌ی یک استخر و پنج جای غذاخوری"},"asks":{"en":"Section 1 gives two short everyday texts: a list of promises a sports centre makes to its customers, and five short descriptions of cafés and restaurants. The questions test rules, times and what each place offers.","tr":"Section 1 iki kısa günlük metin verir: bir spor merkezinin müşterilerine verdiği sözlerin listesi ve kafe ile restoranlar hakkında beş kısa tanıtım. Sorular kuralları, saatleri ve her yerin ne sunduğunu ölçer.","fa":"Section 1 دو متن کوتاه روزمره می‌دهد: فهرست قول‌هایی که یک مرکز ورزشی به مشتری‌هایش می‌دهد و پنج معرفی کوتاه از کافه‌ها و رستوران‌ها. سؤال‌ها قانون‌ها، ساعت‌ها و چیزی را که هر جا ارائه می‌دهد می‌سنجند."},"fields":["Standards","Safety","Changes","Refunds","Payment","Opening times","Booking","Food and drink"],"words":[{"a":"at least","b":"no fewer than / a minimum of","tr":"en az","fa":"دست‌کم"},{"a":"in advance","b":"before it happens / ahead of time","tr":"önceden","fa":"از قبل"},{"a":"refund","b":"your money back","tr":"para iadesi","fa":"بازپرداخت پول"},{"a":"replacement","b":"another one instead","tr":"yerine yenisi","fa":"جایگزین"},{"a":"cashless","b":"cards only / no cash","tr":"nakitsiz","fa":"بدون پول نقد"},{"a":"essential to book","b":"you must reserve","tr":"rezervasyon şart","fa":"رزرو الزامی"},{"a":"takeaway","b":"to take with you","tr":"paket, götürmek üzere","fa":"بیرون‌بر"},{"a":"good value","b":"not expensive for what you get","tr":"fiyatına göre iyi","fa":"به‌صرفه"},{"a":"customers comment on","b":"people who eat there say","tr":"müşteriler ... hakkında yorum yapıyor","fa":"مشتری‌ها درباره‌ی ... نظر می‌دهند"},{"a":"until midnight","b":"late at night","tr":"gece yarısına kadar","fa":"تا نیمه‌شب"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"The equipment is inspected daily\" is not \"the equipment is repaired daily\". One different verb makes the statement FALSE.","tr":"\"Ekipman her gün denetlenir\", \"ekipman her gün onarılır\" demek değildir. Tek bir farklı fiil ifadeyi FALSE yapar.","fa":"«وسایل هر روز بازرسی می‌شوند» با «وسایل هر روز تعمیر می‌شوند» یکی نیست. یک فعلِ متفاوت جمله را FALSE می‌کند."},{"en":"In a matching task a place can be the answer twice, and another place not at all. Check every statement against all five texts.","tr":"Eşleştirmede bir yer iki kez cevap olabilir, başka bir yer hiç olmayabilir. Her ifadeyi beş metnin hepsiyle karşılaştır.","fa":"در تمرین جورکردن یک جا ممکن است دو بار جواب باشد و جای دیگر هیچ‌بار. هر جمله را با هر پنج متن مقایسه کن."}],"example":{"text":"\"Bookings are not necessary, but groups of more than eight should call ahead.\"","item":"Statement: Everyone must book a table. TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"Only large groups should call; bookings are \"not necessary\" for everyone else.","tr":"Yalnızca büyük grupların araması gerekiyor; diğerleri için rezervasyon \"gerekli değil\".","fa":"فقط گروه‌های بزرگ باید زنگ بزنند؛ برای بقیه رزرو «لازم نیست»."}}},{"id":"GT1-notices","ctx":["GT1-notices"],"title":{"en":"Notices, rules and FAQs","tr":"Duyurular, kurallar ve SSS","fa":"اطلاعیه، قانون و پرسش‌های متداول"},"asks":{"en":"Notices, rules and frequently asked questions for a service: a tram, a leisure centre, a block of flats, a competition. Questions test rules, conditions, dates and exceptions.","tr":"Bir hizmet için duyurular, kurallar ve sık sorulan sorular: tramvay, spor merkezi, apartman, yarışma. Sorular kuralları, koşulları, tarihleri ve istisnaları sınar.","fa":"اطلاعیه، قانون و پرسش‌های متداول برای یک خدمت: تراموا، مرکز ورزشی، یک ساختمان مسکونی، یک مسابقه. سؤال‌ها قانون‌ها، شرط‌ها، تاریخ‌ها و استثناها را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["Passengers must buy a ticket before boarding.","Children under five travel free.","Refunds are given for delays of over 30 minutes.","Residents may leave bicycles in the hallway."],"words":[{"a":"must","b":"are required to","tr":"zorunda","fa":"باید"},{"a":"not allowed","b":"prohibited / not permitted","tr":"yasak","fa":"ممنوع"},{"a":"within 14 days","b":"in less than two weeks","tr":"14 gün içinde","fa":"ظرف ۱۴ روز"},{"a":"can claim","b":"are entitled to / are eligible for","tr":"talep edebilir","fa":"می‌تواند درخواست کند"},{"a":"apply","b":"submit a form","tr":"başvurmak","fa":"درخواست دادن"},{"a":"proof","b":"a receipt / evidence of","tr":"kanıt","fa":"مدرک"},{"a":"residents","b":"people living in the building","tr":"sakinler","fa":"ساکنان"},{"a":"compensation","b":"money for a problem you had","tr":"tazminat","fa":"غرامت"},{"a":"beforehand","b":"in advance","tr":"önceden","fa":"از قبل"},{"a":"except","b":"apart from / with the exception of","tr":"hariç","fa":"به‌جز"},{"a":"responsible for","b":"must take care of","tr":"... -den sorumlu","fa":"مسئولِ"},{"a":"on request","b":"if you ask","tr":"talep üzerine","fa":"در صورت درخواست"}],"traps":[{"en":"Exceptions: \"all passengers must..., except season-ticket holders\". A statement about everyone may be FALSE.","tr":"İstisnalar: \"bütün yolcular ... zorunda, abonman sahipleri hariç\". Herkes hakkındaki bir ifade FALSE olabilir.","fa":"استثناها: «همه‌ی مسافران باید...، به‌جز دارندگان بلیت فصلی». جمله‌ای درباره‌ی همه ممکن است FALSE باشد."},{"en":"Numbers in conditions: \"30 minutes or more\" and \"over 30 minutes\" are not the same.","tr":"Koşullardaki sayılar: \"30 dakika veya daha fazla\" ile \"30 dakikadan fazla\" aynı değildir.","fa":"عددها در شرط‌ها: «۳۰ دقیقه یا بیشتر» با «بیش از ۳۰ دقیقه» یکی نیست."}],"example":{"text":"Delay Repay: if your train arrives 30 minutes or more late, you can claim 50% of your ticket price. Claims must be made within 28 days of travel.","item":"Statement: Passengers can claim the full price of their ticket.  (TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"The notice says 50%, which contradicts \"the full price\".","tr":"Duyuru %50 diyor; bu \"tam fiyat\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"اطلاعیه می‌گوید ۵۰٪، که با «قیمت کامل» در تضاد است."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-notices"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-notices","n":22,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 22 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 22’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۲ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}},{"id":"GT1-reviews","ctx":["GT1-reviews"],"title":{"en":"Product and service reviews","tr":"Ürün ve hizmet değerlendirmeleri","fa":"نقد و معرفی کالا و خدمات"},"asks":{"en":"Short reviews or descriptions A-F of products or places: sleeping bags, kitchen machines, cafes, hotels, phone apps. Questions ask which one has a feature, or which review says something.","tr":"Ürünler ya da yerler hakkında A-F harfli kısa değerlendirmeler veya tanıtımlar: uyku tulumları, mutfak aletleri, kafeler, oteller, telefon uygulamaları. Sorular hangisinin bir özelliği olduğunu ya da hangi yorumun bir şey söylediğini sorar.","fa":"نقدها یا معرفی‌های کوتاه A تا F درباره‌ی کالاها یا مکان‌ها: کیسه‌خواب، وسایل آشپزخانه، کافه، هتل، اپلیکیشن. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند کدام یک ویژگی را دارد، یا کدام نقد چیزی را می‌گوید."},"fields":["Which sleeping bag is the lightest?","Which cafe has outdoor seating?","Which app works without the internet?","Which hotel is suitable for families?"],"words":[{"a":"lightweight","b":"weighs very little / easy to carry","tr":"hafif","fa":"سبک"},{"a":"durable","b":"lasts for years / hard-wearing","tr":"dayanıklı","fa":"بادوام"},{"a":"value for money","b":"a good price for what you get","tr":"fiyatına değer","fa":"به‌صرفه"},{"a":"noisy","b":"loud","tr":"gürültülü","fa":"پرسروصدا"},{"a":"spacious","b":"lots of room","tr":"ferah","fa":"جادار"},{"a":"easy to clean","b":"wipes clean","tr":"kolay temizlenir","fa":"راحت تمیز می‌شود"},{"a":"offline","b":"without an internet connection","tr":"çevrimdışı","fa":"آفلاین"},{"a":"outdoor seating","b":"tables outside","tr":"dışarıda oturma yeri","fa":"میز در فضای باز"},{"a":"guarantee","b":"free repairs for two years","tr":"garanti","fa":"گارانتی"},{"a":"compact","b":"small / takes up little space","tr":"küçük, kompakt","fa":"جمع‌وجور"},{"a":"fully booked","b":"no rooms left","tr":"tamamen dolu","fa":"کاملاً پر"},{"a":"suitable for families","b":"children welcome / cots available","tr":"ailelere uygun","fa":"مناسب خانواده"}],"traps":[{"en":"Superlatives: \"the lightest\" needs a comparison with all the others, not just the word \"light\".","tr":"Üstünlük sıfatları: \"en hafif\" diğerlerinin hepsiyle karşılaştırma ister, yalnızca \"hafif\" kelimesi yetmez.","fa":"صفت عالی: «سبک‌ترین» یعنی مقایسه با همه‌ی بقیه، نه فقط کلمه‌ی «سبک»."},{"en":"A review may mention a feature only to say that it is missing.","tr":"Bir yorum bir özellikten yalnızca eksik olduğunu söylemek için bahsedebilir.","fa":"یک نقد ممکن است به ویژگی‌ای فقط اشاره کند تا بگوید ندارد."}],"example":{"text":"A  The Trekker 200 weighs 900 g and packs down small.\nB  The Summit weighs just 650 g, though it is not quite as warm.\nC  The Polar Pro is the warmest of the three, at 1.4 kg.","item":"Which sleeping bag is the lightest?","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Compare all three: 650 g is less than 900 g and 1.4 kg.","tr":"Üçünü de karşılaştır: 650 g, 900 g ve 1,4 kg’dan az.","fa":"هر سه را مقایسه کن: ۶۵۰ گرم از ۹۰۰ گرم و ۱٫۴ کیلو کمتر است."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-reviews"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-reviews","n":19,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Statements, then matching","tr":"Önce ifadeler, sonra eşleştirme","fa":"اول جمله‌ها، بعد جورکردن"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-6 are TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN statements about the first text. Questions 7-14 ask which of five places, A-E, each statement is true for. A letter can be the answer more than once.","tr":"Soru 1-6 ilk metinle ilgili TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN ifadeleridir. Soru 7-14 her ifadenin beş yerden (A-E) hangisi için doğru olduğunu sorar. Bir harf birden fazla kez cevap olabilir.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۶ جمله‌های TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN درباره‌ی متن اول‌اند. سؤال‌های ۷ تا ۱۴ می‌پرسند هر جمله درباره‌ی کدام یک از پنج مکان (A تا E) درست است. یک حرف می‌تواند بیش از یک بار جواب باشد."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"One key idea per statement","tr":"Her ifadede bir anahtar fikir","fa":"در هر جمله یک ایده‌ی کلیدی"},"steps":[{"en":"Underline the key idea of the statement: a discount, a time, a payment rule.","tr":"İfadenin anahtar fikrinin altını çiz: bir indirim, bir saat, bir ödeme kuralı.","fa":"زیر ایده‌ی کلیدی جمله خط بکش: تخفیف، ساعت، قانون پرداخت."},{"en":"Think of other ways to say it: \"no cash\" = cards only; \"reserve\" = book.","tr":"Başka nasıl söylenebileceğini düşün: \"no cash\" = cards only; \"reserve\" = book.","fa":"فکر کن چطور می‌شود جور دیگری گفتش: «no cash» یعنی cards only؛ «reserve» یعنی book."},{"en":"Scan all five listings for that idea. Do not stop at the first place that seems close.","tr":"Beş ilanın hepsinde o fikri ara. Yakın görünen ilk yerde durma.","fa":"همه‌ی پنج معرفی را برای آن ایده نگاه کن. در اولین جایی که نزدیک به نظر می‌رسد نایست."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Who is speaking?","tr":"Kim söylüyor?","fa":"چه کسی می‌گوید؟"},"body":{"en":"A listing can report what customers say as well as what the business offers. If a statement says \"customers praise\", look for the customers’ view, not the owner’s description.","tr":"Bir ilan, işletmenin sunduklarının yanında müşterilerin ne dediğini de aktarabilir. İfade \"müşteriler övüyor\" diyorsa, sahibinin tanıtımını değil müşterilerin görüşünü ara.","fa":"یک معرفی ممکن است علاوه بر چیزی که کسب‌وکار ارائه می‌دهد، حرف مشتری‌ها را هم نقل کند. اگر جمله می‌گوید «مشتری‌ها تعریف می‌کنند»، دنبال نظر مشتری‌ها بگرد، نه توضیحِ صاحب کار."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One matching statement, step by step","tr":"Bir eşleştirme ifadesi, adım adım","fa":"یک جمله‌ی جورکردنی، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Which place is this statement true for? Write the correct letter, A-C.","text":"\"A Corner Bakery: fresh bread daily; cash only. B Harbour Grill: open until 11 pm. C Bean Stop: coffee and cakes; free Wi-Fi for customers.\"","item":"You can use the internet here.","answer":"C","walk":[{"en":"Key idea: using the internet.","tr":"Anahtar fikir: interneti kullanmak.","fa":"ایده‌ی کلیدی: استفاده از اینترنت."},{"en":"Other words for it: Wi-Fi, online, connection.","tr":"Başka kelimelerle: Wi-Fi, online, bağlantı.","fa":"کلمه‌های دیگرش: Wi-Fi، آنلاین، اتصال."},{"en":"Only C mentions free Wi-Fi: write C.","tr":"Yalnızca C ücretsiz Wi-Fi’den söz ediyor: C yaz.","fa":"فقط C از Wi-Fi رایگان حرف می‌زند: C را بنویس."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"Towels are available at reception.\" Statement: \"Towels cost two pounds each.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["NOT GIVEN","TRUE","FALSE"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"The text says where towels are, not what they cost.","tr":"Metin havluların nerede olduğunu söylüyor, fiyatını değil.","fa":"متن می‌گوید حوله کجاست، نه اینکه چقدر قیمت دارد."}},"remember":{"en":"One key idea per statement. Check all five places, and remember a letter can be used twice.","tr":"Her ifadede bir anahtar fikir. Beş yerin hepsine bak ve bir harfin iki kez kullanılabileceğini unutma.","fa":"هر جمله یک ایده‌ی کلیدی دارد. هر پنج مکان را نگاه کن و یادت باشد یک حرف می‌تواند دو بار بیاید."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x02-r1-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 1","title":{"en":"A pool and places to eat","tr":"Bir havuz ve yemek yerleri","fa":"یک استخر و جاهای غذاخوری"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT1-notices","GT1-reviews"],"texts":[{"title":"Brookside Leisure Pool: our customer charter","kind":"customer charter","body":"This charter sets out the standards you can expect every time you visit Brookside Leisure Pool. In our last customer survey, cleanliness was rated as the most important thing about a visit, so we have put it first.\n\nCleanliness\nOur changing rooms are checked every hour and fully cleaned at least four times a day. If you notice a problem between checks, please tell any member of staff and we will deal with it straight away.\n\nSafety\nAt least two qualified lifeguards are on duty at all times during public swimming sessions. During lessons and club sessions, the instructor or coach is responsible for safety at the side of the pool.\n\nTimetable changes\nWe sometimes need to close part of the pool for competitions or maintenance. Any change to the timetable will be announced at least seven days in advance, both on our website and on the noticeboard in the entrance hall.\n\nLessons\nIf we have to cancel a swimming lesson, you will receive a full refund or a free replacement lesson, whichever you prefer. Unfortunately, we cannot refund lessons that you are unable to attend.\n\nAccess\nThe main pool has a poolside hoist for swimmers who need help getting in and out of the water. Please ask at reception when you arrive, and a member of staff will set it up for you.\n\nLockers\nLockers in the changing rooms take a one-pound coin, which is returned to you when you open the locker again. Please do not leave valuables on the benches.\n\nComments and complaints\nWe welcome all comments. Written complaints will receive a full reply within ten working days. If you would rather talk to someone, leave your phone number and the duty manager will call you back, usually on the same day."},{"title":"Eating near Kingsford Station","kind":"five listings","body":"A  The Platform Café\nRight opposite the main entrance, this small café opens at 6 am, making it the obvious choice for an early breakfast before a train. The coffee is excellent and everything can be taken away. Show a valid rail ticket at the counter and you will get ten per cent off your order. There are only eight tables, and bookings are not taken. If you are in a hurry, you can order through the café's app and collect your order from the counter without queuing.\n\nB  Lucia's Kitchen\nA family-run restaurant five minutes' walk from the station, Lucia's makes fresh pasta every morning. There is a separate menu for under-twelves, with smaller portions at half price. The restaurant is very popular on Friday and Saturday evenings, so it is essential to book a table if you plan to come at the weekend. Closed on Mondays.\n\nC  Green Bowl\nThis bright vegetarian café serves salads, soups and grain bowls, with plenty of choice for vegans. In good weather you can sit on the terrace overlooking the canal. Please note that Green Bowl is a cashless business: cards and phone payments only. Open for lunch only, from 11.30 am to 3 pm.\n\nD  The Signal Box\nUntil the 1980s this building controlled the trains coming in and out of Kingsford; today it is a lively pub with a large garden. There is live music every Thursday, and dogs are welcome both inside and in the garden. Food is served until 9 pm.\n\nE  Spice Junction\nSpice Junction offers a good-value set lunch on weekdays and a full menu in the evening. It stays open until midnight from Thursday to Saturday, so it is ideal after a late train. Customers regularly comment on how quickly the food arrives, even when the restaurant is full. Most dishes can be made less spicy on request, and the staff are happy to explain the menu."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 1-6. Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text? Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The changing rooms are cleaned every hour.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"checked every hour and fully cleaned at least four times a day","why":{"en":"They are checked every hour, but cleaned \"at least four times a day\".","tr":"Her saat kontrol ediliyor ama \"günde en az dört kez\" temizleniyor.","fa":"هر ساعت بررسی می‌شوند، اما «دست‌کم چهار بار در روز» تمیز می‌شوند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":2,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"There is always more than one lifeguard on duty during public swimming.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"At least two qualified lifeguards are on duty at all times during public swimming sessions","why":{"en":"\"At least two... at all times\" = always more than one.","tr":"\"Her zaman en az iki\" = her zaman birden fazla.","fa":"«دست‌کم دو نفر... در همه‌ی زمان‌ها» یعنی همیشه بیش از یک نفر."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":3,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Changes to the timetable are announced only on the website.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"both on our website and on the noticeboard in the entrance hall","why":{"en":"They are announced \"both on our website and on the noticeboard\".","tr":"\"Hem web sitemizde hem de duyuru panosunda\" duyuruluyor.","fa":"«هم در وب‌سایت و هم روی تابلوی اعلانات» اعلام می‌شوند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":4,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Most complaints that the pool receives are about the water temperature.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"cleanliness was rated as the most important thing about a visit","why":{"en":"The survey is about what matters most to customers. Nothing is said about the subject of complaints.","tr":"Anket müşteriler için en önemli şeyle ilgili. Şikâyetlerin konusu hakkında hiçbir şey yok.","fa":"نظرسنجی درباره‌ی مهم‌ترین چیز برای مشتری‌هاست. درباره‌ی موضوع شکایت‌ها چیزی گفته نشده."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","PARA-research"]},{"n":5,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Customers get their money back if the pool cancels a lesson.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"If we have to cancel a swimming lesson, you will receive a full refund","why":{"en":"A full refund (or a free replacement lesson) when the pool cancels.","tr":"Havuz iptal ederse tam iade (ya da ücretsiz telafi dersi).","fa":"اگر استخر لغو کند، کل پول برمی‌گردد (یا یک جلسه‌ی جایگزین رایگان)."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":6,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The lockers are big enough for a large sports bag.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"Lockers in the changing rooms take a one-pound coin","why":{"en":"The text says how the lockers work, not how big they are.","tr":"Metin dolapların nasıl çalıştığını söylüyor, ne kadar büyük olduklarını değil.","fa":"متن می‌گوید کمدها چطور کار می‌کنند، نه اینکه چقدر بزرگ‌اند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 7-14. Look at the five places to eat, A-E, in the text. For which place is each of the following statements true? Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 7-14 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-features","bank":["A The Platform Café","B Lucia’s Kitchen","C Green Bowl","D The Signal Box","E Spice Junction"],"questions":[{"n":7,"kind":"match","prompt":"You can get a discount by showing a train ticket.","correct":0,"evidence":"Show a valid rail ticket at the counter and you will get ten per cent off","why":{"en":"A: \"Show a valid rail ticket... ten per cent off\".","tr":"A: \"Geçerli bir tren biletini gösterirsen... yüzde on indirim\".","fa":"A: «بلیت قطار معتبر را نشان بده... ده درصد تخفیف»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":8,"kind":"match","prompt":"Cash is not accepted.","correct":2,"evidence":"Green Bowl is a cashless business","why":{"en":"C: \"a cashless business: cards and phone payments only\".","tr":"C: \"nakitsiz bir işletme: yalnızca kart ve telefonla ödeme\".","fa":"C: «کسب‌وکاری بدون پول نقد: فقط کارت و پرداخت با گوشی»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":9,"kind":"match","prompt":"You need to reserve a table if you want to eat there at the weekend.","correct":1,"evidence":"it is essential to book a table if you plan to come at the weekend","why":{"en":"B: \"essential to book a table\" at the weekend. A does not take bookings at all.","tr":"B: hafta sonu \"masa ayırtmak şart\". A hiç rezervasyon almıyor.","fa":"B: آخر هفته «رزرو میز الزامی است». A اصلاً رزرو قبول نمی‌کند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase","TR-detail"]},{"n":10,"kind":"match","prompt":"It is open late at night on certain days.","correct":4,"evidence":"It stays open until midnight from Thursday to Saturday","why":{"en":"E: \"until midnight from Thursday to Saturday\". D serves food until 9 pm only.","tr":"E: \"Perşembeden cumartesiye gece yarısına kadar\". D yalnızca 21.00’e kadar yemek veriyor.","fa":"E: «از پنجشنبه تا شنبه تا نیمه‌شب». D فقط تا ساعت ۹ شب غذا می‌دهد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":11,"kind":"match","prompt":"Customers praise how fast the food is served.","correct":4,"evidence":"Customers regularly comment on how quickly the food arrives","why":{"en":"E: this is what customers say, \"how quickly the food arrives\". E is used twice.","tr":"E: bu müşterilerin söylediği, \"yemeğin ne kadar çabuk geldiği\". E iki kez kullanılıyor.","fa":"E: این حرفِ مشتری‌هاست، «غذا چقدر سریع می‌رسد». E دو بار به کار می‌رود."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":12,"kind":"match","prompt":"Animals are allowed inside.","correct":3,"evidence":"dogs are welcome both inside and in the garden","why":{"en":"D: \"dogs are welcome both inside and in the garden\".","tr":"D: \"köpekler hem içeride hem bahçede kabul ediliyor\".","fa":"D: «سگ‌ها هم داخل و هم در باغ پذیرفته می‌شوند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":13,"kind":"match","prompt":"The building once had a different use.","correct":3,"evidence":"Until the 1980s this building controlled the trains","why":{"en":"D: it \"controlled the trains\" until the 1980s; today it is a pub.","tr":"D: 1980’lere kadar \"trenleri yönetiyordu\"; bugün bir pub.","fa":"D: تا دهه‌ی ۱۹۸۰ «قطارها را کنترل می‌کرد»؛ امروز یک پاب است."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":14,"kind":"match","prompt":"There is a separate menu for children.","correct":1,"evidence":"There is a separate menu for under-twelves","why":{"en":"B: \"a separate menu for under-twelves\" = children.","tr":"B: \"on iki yaş altı için ayrı menü\" = çocuklar.","fa":"B: «منوی جداگانه برای زیر دوازده سال» یعنی بچه‌ها."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]}],"id":"c-x02-r1-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The shop is cashless.\" This means customers...","options":["do not have to pay","must pay in cash","cannot pay with notes and coins"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Cashless = no cash: cards or phone only.","tr":"Cashless = nakit yok: yalnızca kart ya da telefon.","fa":"cashless یعنی بدون پول نقد: فقط کارت یا گوشی."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":2,"prompt":"A statement says \"You must reserve a table.\" Which words in a listing mean the same?","options":["bookings are not taken","it is essential to book","tables are available"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Essential to book = you must reserve.","tr":"Essential to book = rezervasyon yapmak zorunlu.","fa":"essential to book یعنی باید رزرو کنی."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Five places, eight statements, and \"NB You may use any letter more than once\". What does this tell you?","options":["some places will be the answer more than once","each place is used exactly once","three statements have no answer"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Eight statements and five letters: at least one letter must come up twice.","tr":"Sekiz ifade ve beş harf: en az bir harf iki kez çıkmalı.","fa":"هشت جمله و پنج حرف: دست‌کم یک حرف باید دو بار بیاید."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"A listing says \"Customers say the portions are huge.\" Statement: \"The restaurant advertises large portions.\" Do they mean the same?","options":["Yes, exactly the same","They are opposites","No: it is the customers’ view, not the restaurant’s"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Check whose words they are: the customers’, not the restaurant’s.","tr":"Kimin sözü olduğuna bak: restoranın değil, müşterilerin.","fa":"ببین حرفِ چه کسی است: مشتری‌ها، نه رستوران."}},{"tests":"trap","point":1,"prompt":"Text: \"Repairs are reported to the council within 48 hours.\" Statement: \"The council hears about repairs within two days.\"","options":["FALSE","TRUE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"48 hours = two days: the same fact in other words.","tr":"48 saat = iki gün: aynı bilgi başka kelimelerle.","fa":"۴۸ ساعت یعنی دو روز: همان واقعیت با کلمه‌های دیگر."}}],"id":"c-x02-r1-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-02","unit":"x02-r1"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
